    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-many-platforms-are-not-a-1": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-many-platforms-are-not-a-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Many platforms are not a single repository: they're a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "root directory holding N service repos",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "auth-service/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "billing-service/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", …), with or without git at the root itself. Archon models this as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "folder project",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a directory for which Archon applies no git machinery (no managed worktree, branch or pull request), whether or not it is a git repository. Folder projects also fit a single repository you want to run in place, or a business-operations folder with no git at all. They get identity, per-project env vars, run history and artifact storage like repo projects. Register the root once, and every workflow and chat runs "
        },
        {
          "insert": "in place",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " at that root by default, so the agent sees all contained repos at once. Opt into overlay-isolated, approval-gated container execution with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--container",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (see the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Container isolation guide",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/30-authoring/20-guides/70-container-isolation.md",
              "label": "Container isolation guide"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ")."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-register-the-root-2": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-register-the-root-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Register the root"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-from-the-multi-repo-root-3": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-from-the-multi-repo-root-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "From the multi-repo root, run any workflow with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--folder",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The first run registers the folder project; later runs from the root or ordinary subdirectories need no flag. For cross-service runs, start at the registered folder root or pass "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--cwd ~/platform",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Running from inside a nested Git service repository resolves that service as its own repository project and registers it on first use."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-bash-4": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-bash-4",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "bash"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "cd ~/platform          # contains auth-service/, billing-service/, ... — with or without git at the root\narchon workflow run archon-investigate --folder \"How do these services call each other?\"\n# → Registered folder project \"platform\" (~/platform)\n# → Folder project — running in place (no worktree isolation)."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-you-can-also-register-fr-5": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-you-can-also-register-fr-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "You can also register from chat ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "/register-project --folder platform ~/platform",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") or the web console's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Add Project",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (choose "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Local path",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", paste the path and select "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Register as a folder project",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). These choices work for git roots too. Without an explicit choice, web and chat auto-detect non-git paths as folders and git paths as repos. An existing repo registration is not converted."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-how-work-happens-across-6": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-how-work-happens-across-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "How work happens across repos"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-agent-s-working-di-7": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-agent-s-working-di-7",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The agent's working directory is the root",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so it can "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cd",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " into any child repo, read across services, and make coordinated changes in one run."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-per-service-git-is-the-8": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-per-service-git-is-the-8",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Per-service git is the agent's job.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Archon does not create a worktree or manage branches/PRs for a folder project: the agent runs "
        },
        {
          "insert": "git",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "/"
        },
        {
          "insert": "gh",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " itself inside each service repo (branch, commit, push, open PR). Your workflow prompts should instruct it to do so per service."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-chat-status-comma-9": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-chat-status-comma-9",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The chat "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " command and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon doctor",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " list the contained repos so you can confirm what's in scope:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-text-10": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-text-10",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "text"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Contains 20 git repos: auth-service, billing-service, … (+10 more)"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-artifacts-and-logs-are-s-11": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-artifacts-and-logs-are-s-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Artifacts and logs are stored under "
        },
        {
          "insert": "~/.archon/workspaces/_folder/<slug>/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and per-project "
        },
        {
          "insert": "env vars",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "docs/30-authoring/10-getting-started/35-configuration.md",
              "label": "env vars"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " work exactly as for repo projects."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-when-you-want-isolation-12": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-when-you-want-isolation-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When you want isolation for one service"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-folder-projects-intentio-13": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-folder-projects-intentio-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Folder projects intentionally run in the live checkout: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--branch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--from",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " are rejected, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/worktree",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " reports \"not applicable\". If you want Archon-managed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worktree isolation",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for a single service (an isolated branch per run, auto PR flow), register that service repo as its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "own",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " project:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-bash-14": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-bash-14",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "bash"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "cd ~/platform/auth-service       # a real git repo\narchon workflow run archon-implement --branch fix-auth \"Fix the token refresh bug\"\n# → normal repo project: isolated worktree + branch, no --folder"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-two-models-compose-15": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-the-two-models-compose-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The two models compose: keep the root registered as a folder project for cross-service work, and register individual services as repo projects when you want per-run isolation for just that service."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-not-a-fit-for-16": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-not-a-fit-for-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Not a fit for"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-archon-managed-branchi-17": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-archon-managed-branchi-17",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Archon-managed branching/PRs spanning child repos",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the agent coordinates git across services itself; Archon does not create a composed multi-repo worktree (a future isolation backend may)."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-65-multi-repo-projects-a-repo-you-want-isolat-18": {
      "id": "b-65-multi-repo-projects-a-repo-you-want-isolat-18",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A repo you want isolated per run",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": register "
        },
        {
          "insert": "that repo",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " directly (repo project), not the parent folder."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
